{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Coreference Resolution Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: pretrained neural coreference (AllenNLP / spaCy-experimental)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import spacy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "nlp = spacy.load(\"en_coreference_web_trf\")   # experimental model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "doc = nlp(\"Apple announced new products. The company said they would ship soon.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for cluster in doc._.coref_clusters:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(cluster, \"->\", [m.text for m in cluster])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "On a longer document, you get something like:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Cluster 1: [Apple, The company, they]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- Cluster 2: [new products]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: rule-based pronoun resolver (teaching)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/main.py` for a stdlib-only implementation:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1. Extract mentions: named entities (capitalized spans), pronouns (dict lookup), definite descriptions (\"the X\")."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "2. For each pronoun, look at the previous K mentions and score them by:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "   - gender/number agreement (heuristic)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "   - recency (closer wins)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "   - syntactic role (subjects preferred)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "3. Link the highest-scoring antecedent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Not competitive with neural models. But it shows the search space and the decisions an end-to-end model must make."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: using LLMs for coreference"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "prompt = f\"\"\"Text: {text}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "List every pronoun and noun phrase that refers to a person or company."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Cluster them by what they refer to. Output JSON:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "[{{\"entity\": \"Apple\", \"mentions\": [\"Apple\", \"the company\", \"it\"]}}, ...]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Two failure modes to watch. First, LLMs over-merge (\"him\" and \"her\" referring to two distinct people). Second, LLMs silently drop mentions in long documents. Always verify with span-offset checks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: evaluation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The standard conll-2012 script computes MUC, B\u00b3, CEAF-\u03c64 and reports the average. For an in-house eval, start with span-level precision and recall on your annotated test set, then add mention-linking F1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run the rule-based resolver in `code/main.py` on 5 hand-crafted paragraphs. Measure mention-link accuracy against ground truth.\n2. **Medium.** Use a pretrained neural coref model on a news article. Compare clusters against your own manual annotation. Where did it fail?\n3. **Hard.** Build a coref-enhanced NER pipeline: NER first, then merge via coref clusters. Measure entity-coverage improvement vs NER-only on 100 articles."
      ]
    }
  ],
